      "taskType": "errorAnalysis",
      "representation": "graph",
      "prompt": "A student says, “This relation is NOT a function because two plotted points have the same output.” Use the displayed graph and the vertical-line test to classify the relation and correct the student's claim.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "answer",
          "label": "Classification",
          "inputProfile": "choice",
          "expected": "function"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Repeated outputs are allowed; repeated inputs with different outputs are not.",
        "reasoning": [
          "The plotted inputs {{x1}}, {{x2}}, and {{x3}} are all different even though two points share output {{y}}.",
          "No vertical line hits more than one plotted point, so each input has exactly one output and the relation is a function."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "FUNCTION"
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Apply the vertical-line test to the x-values. Sharing a y-value does not violate the function rule."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Different x-values may share the same y-value. Look only for whether one x-value is paired with two different y-values."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "x1": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -8,
            "max": -3
          },
          "x2": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -2,
            "max": 2
          },
          "x3": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 3,
            "max": 8
          },
